s a max  proficiency rank of 10.  once this is achieved you'll no longer  be earning xp from this item towards  your expertise level  so for the most efficient gains towards  your expertise level you would try to  change out your gear and weapons as soon  as they have reached maximum proficiency  to run something that hasn't been  leveled  like i mentioned above the gaining of  expertise level will provide you with  points to upgrade an item  depending on the item type the upgrade  gained from using one of these points is  one of the following  weapons one percent increase to base  damage  gear one percent increase to base armor  value  skills one percent increase to base  damage healing status effect duration  but they made sure to note that these  values are a work in progress  so for balancing purposes they may be  tweaked before release  summing up gear weapon and skills now  have a new ranking system that we can  use to level up through using them in  normal gameplay  leveling up items will increase your  overall expertise level in turn granting  you something that you can use to  increase the base stats of an item of  your choosing  these couple of lines are quite  important to note  for each level of expertise players gain  increased ability to upgrade an item  using materials  players may upgrade any given item as  many times as their current expertise  level this basically means that you can  pump all of the upgrade points into a  single piece of gear in theory  sadly all i can see is some potential  balancing issues coming from this  imagine a striker drone that could mow  down everything on the field  a sniper build with insane levels of  damage though to be fair this probably  wouldn't be a good use of the upgrades  any half decent sniper build can already  kill most enemies in one shot but the  numbers would look pretty impressive  i'm sure they're already considering  this and are working through the testing  as we speak  they might add depreciating gains with  each additional point  or introduce a cap on the number of  upgrades a single piece can have  maybe the points received will be locked  into an item category forcing you to  upgrade gear weapons and skills rather  than just focusing on one type  naturally there is a finite number of  items so there will be a max expertise  level but as new items are added that  max level will increase  we also need to think about the fact  that we don't know how many items need  to be leveled to max proficiency in  order to gain an expertise level again  i'm sure this is something that they're  still working out  i actually think this isn't a bad idea  or at the very least it will be more  widely accepted than simply raising the  max gear score level  people who like to grind will have a lot  more to do  those who like to min max will have a  little bit of extra to work on to get  the absolute best out of their build  i certainly don't think this will affect  build diversity and i actually don't  think this was the intention  while you'll be using weapons and gear  that you don't usually touch for a small  amount of time when they're at max  proficiency it's likely they'll be  tossed aside again returning to your  favorites  your most used build will be getting  stronger but everything else will stay  as it is  as i said at the beginning we don't have  all the information on this yet just  what was in the intelligence annex but  the discussions i've been seeing were  shown that a lot of people weren't quite  understanding  i'll post the article in the description  if you haven't checked it out yet  i suspect balancing and testing is  likely to affect the outcome of some of  the points raised so expect some changes  before next year  i'll probably remake this once the  update has been released and the finer  details have been sorted  but as always until more content is  added to the game this won't be enough  to have people return on its own  we need to remember though these  intelligence annex releases are just  giving us small snippets of what's  coming  these annex updates don't represent the  bulk of what we'll be seeing  anyway i hope you've cleared up a few  things with this video if you have any  further questions regarding expertise  and how it currently stands let me know  in the comments i'll do my best to get  back to you  cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  uh  you

